        "content": "0: \"\"\"Base class for MCP-client integrations exposed in the RLM kernel.\n92: def _resolve_streamable_http():\n93:     \"\"\"Return an SDK streamable-HTTP transport callable.\n95:     SDK versions vary: some expose ``streamablehttp_client(url, headers=...)``,\n96:     others ``streamable_http_client(url, *, http_client=...)``, and some expose\n100:     from mcp.client import streamable_http as mod  # noqa: PLC0415\n102:     for name in (\"streamablehttp_client\", \"streamable_http_client\"):\n107:         \"the installed `mcp` SDK exposes no streamable-HTTP client; upgrade `mcp`\"\n206:         \"\"\"Open an initialized MCP ClientSession bound to ``stack``.\n208:         Override for non-HTTP transports (e.g. stdio). The default connects over\n209:         streamable HTTP with a Bearer token from auth.json. The URL comes from the\n214:         from mcp import ClientSession  # noqa: PLC0415\n222:         transport = _resolve_streamable_http()\n226:         # SDK signatures vary: some take headers=, others only http_client=.\n230:         elif \"http_client\" in params:\n231:             import httpx  # noqa: PLC0415\n233:             client = await stack.enter_async_context(httpx.AsyncClient(headers=auth_header))\n234:             cm = transport(url, http_client=client)\n237:                 f\"unsupported mcp streamable-HTTP client signature: {tuple(params)}\"\n241:         session = await stack.enter_async_context(ClientSession(read, write))\n",
