e rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync search(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Search adjacent tiles for hidden passages and traps. Pass `times` to repeat — hidden passages typically need 5-10 searches at the same tile to reveal. Defaults to 1.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== reveal ===\nHelp on function reveal in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync reveal(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Reveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive. The FULL map (x1=0, y1=0, x2=78, y2=20) is a valid request and returns all 79 columns. Returns the sub-rectangle as text; consumes NO game turn. Out-of-range requests are clamped to the grid, and any clamping is stated in the reply.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_eat ===\nHelp on function np_eat in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync np_eat(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Eat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_wield ===\nHelp on function np_wield in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync np_wield(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Wield a weapon.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_wear ===\nHelp on function np_wear in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync np_wear(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Wear a piece of armor.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_read ===\nHelp on function np_read in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync np_read(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Read a scroll, spellbook, or something else.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_apply ===\nHelp on function np_apply in module rlm.mcp_base:\n\nasync np_apply(**kwargs: 'Any') -> 'Any'\n    Apply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.\n    \n    Arguments (JSON Schema):\n    {}\n\n\n=== np_zap ===\nHelp on function np_zap in module rlm.mcp_base