s a gap/door in the wall\n  y7: (34, '|')\n  y8: (34, '-') - this is a gap/door in the wall\n  y9: (34, '-') - that's the corner\n- East wall (x41): `|` at y4, `|` at y5, `|` at y6, `|` at y7, `|` at y8\n\n**Lower-left room**: x1-5, y13-17 (walls at x1, x5, y12, y17)\n- North wall (y12): `-` at x1-5\n- South wall (y17): `-` at x1-5\n- West wall (x1): `|` at y13, `|` at y14, `|` at y15, `|` at y16\n- East wall (x5): `|` at y13, `-` at y14, `|` at y15, `-` at y16\n\nI've searched at:\n- (7,2) in starting room → nothing\n- (8,1) near starting room → nothing (20 searches)\n- (5,3) in starting room → nothing (20 searches)\n- (35,4), (36,4), (37,6), (33,6), (35,8) in right room → nothing\n- (20,10), (20,12), (24,11) in middle room → nothing\n- (3,13), (3,15) in lower-left room → nothing\n- (26,10) near middle room → nothing\n\nI have NOT searched at:\n- Near the east wall of the right room (x41) - but I searched at (37,6) which is close\n- Near the south wall of the middle room from inside the room\n- Near the north wall of the lower-left room from inside\n\nWait, let me think about this differently. Searching at a position reveals hidden doors in the 8 adjacent tiles. Let me calculate which wall tiles I've covered:\n\nStarting room searches:\n- (7,2): covers tiles x6-8, y1-3 → covers parts of north, west, and east walls\n- (8,1): covers tiles x7-9, y0-2 → covers north wall, and the corridor\n- (5,3): covers tiles x4-6, y2-4 → covers west wall and part of the room\n\nI haven't covered:\n- (6,4) which would cover tiles x5-7, y3-5 → covers south wall\n- (8,4) which would cover tiles x7-9, y3-5 → covers east wall and south wall\n\nBut the right room is far from the starting room. The corridor from the starting room goes right at x10, down to y6, then right to the right room at x28+.\n\nLet me check: are there any corridors I haven't explored? Let me trace all corridors:\n\n1. (8,0): dead-end above starting room's north door\n2. (3,3)→(3,4)→(3,5)→(3,6)→(4,6)→(5,6): left and down from starting room's west door\n3. (5,6)→(5,7)→(5,8)→(5,9)→(5,10)→(5,11)→(6,11)→(6,12): going down to lower-left room\n   Wait, let me check:\n   y6: (3, '#'), (4, '#'), (5, '#')\n   y7: (5, '#')\n   y8: (5, '#'), (10, '#'), (11, '#'), (12, '#')\n   y9: (5, '#'), (12, '*'), (27, '#'), (32, '#')\n   y10: (5, '#'), (12, '#'), (13, '#'), (14, '#')\n   y11: (5, '#'), (6, '#')\n   y12: (6, '#')\n   \n   So the left corridor goes: (3,3)→(3,4)→(3,5)→(3,6)→(4,6)→(5,6)→(5,7)→(5,8)→(5,9)→(5,10)→(5,11)→(6,11)→(6,12)\n   Then (6,12) connects to (6,13) which goes to the lower-left room.\n   \n   Wait, but at y8, there are also (10, '#'), (11, '#'), (12, '#'). And at y9, (12, '*') which is a gem. So there's a branch at (5,8) or somewhere that goes right to (10,8), (11,8), (12,8) and then to (12,9).\n\n   Actually, let me check: the east corridor from the starting room:\n   (10,2)→(10,3)→(10,4)→(10,5)→(10,6)→(10,7)→(10,8)→(11,8)→(12,8)→(12,9)\n   Then (12,9) has `*` (gem) and connects to... (12,10)? Let me check:\n   y10: (12, '#') → yes, (12,10) is `#`\n   (12,10)→(13,10)→(14,10)→(15,10) which is the west wall of the middle room (but (15,10) is `|` so it's a wall).\n   \n   Wait, but the middle room's west wall has `|` at y10 and `.` at y11. So the corridor enters the middle room through (15,11).\n\n   Actually, looking at the corridor from (12,9): (12,9) is `*` (gem on the ground, not a corridor). Let me check if (12,9) is actually a corridor tile or a room tile. Looking at the map:\n   y9: (5, '#'), (12, '*'), (15, '-'), ... (27, '#'), (32, '#'), (34, '-')\n   \n   The `*` at (12,9) is between the left corridor and the middle room's north wall. It seems like a corridor tile with a gem on it. The corridor goes from (12,8) to (12,9) to (12,10) to (13,10) to (14,10) to the middle room.\n\n4. Right corridor from starting room: (10,2)→(10,3)→...→(10,8)→(11,8)→(12,8)→(12,9)→(12,10)→(13,10)→(14,10)→(15,11) (enters middle room)\n\n5. From the middle room:\n   - West: (15,11)→(14,11)→...→(12,10)→(12,9)→(12,8)→(10,8)→...→(10,2)→starting room\n   - East: (25,10)→(26,10)→...→(32,10)→(32,9)→(32,8)→(33,8)→(34,8) which is the right room's west wall\n     Wait, y10: (25, '-'), (26, '#'), ..., (32, '#')\n     And y9: (32, '#')\n     And y8: (32, '#'), (33, '#'), (34, '-')\n     So (25,10) is `-` (gap in wall), then (26,10)→(27,10)→...→(32,10) are corridors, then (32,9) and (32,8) and (33,8) are corridors, then (34,8) is `-` (gap in right room's west wall).\n\n   Also from (25,12) which is `.` (gap): (26,12)→(27,12) are corridors. And (27,11)→(28,11) are corridors. Let me check:\n   y11: (27, '#'), (28, '#')\n   y12: (26, '#'), (27, '#')\n   \n   So there's a corridor from (25,12) to (26,12) to (27,12) to (27,11) to (28,11) to... where? (28,11) connects to what? Let me check y10: (26, '#'), (27, '#'), ..., (32, '#'). And (27,10) connects to (27,11). So this corridor just connects (25,12) to the main east corridor.\n\n6. From the middle room going left: (15,13)→(14,13)→(13,13)→(12,13)→(12,14)... wait:\n   y13: (12, '#'), (13, '#'), (14, '#')\n   y14: (9, '#'), (10, '#'), (11, '#'), (12, '#')\n   y15: (6, '#'), (7, '#'), (8, '#'), (9, '#')\n   \n   So from (15,13)→(14,13)→(13,13)→(12,13)→(12,14)→(11,14)→(10,14)→(9,14)→(9,15)→(8,15)→(7,15)→(6,15)→(6,14)→(6,13)→(6,12) which connects to the left corridor going up.\n\nSo the corridors form a loop: starting room → left corridor down → lower-left room → corridor right → middle room → corridor right → right room → corridor up → middle room → corridor left → starting room.\n\nAll corridors are explored. All rooms are explored. No stairs down found.\n\nThe only possibility is a hidden door in one of the walls I haven't searched near. Let me check which wall tiles I haven't searched near:\n\nStarting room (x4-8, y1-5):\n- I searched at (7,2), (8,1), (5,3)\n- (7,2) covers adjacent tiles: (6,1),(7,1),(8,1),(6,2),(7,2),(8,2),(6,3),(7,3),(8,3) → covers north wall x6-8, east wall partially\n- (8,1) covers: (7,0),(8,0),(9,0),(7,1),(8,1),(9,1),(7,2),(8,2),(9,2) → covers north wall x7-9, corridor\n- (5,3) covers: (4,2),(5,2),(6,2),(4,3),(5,3),(6,3),(4,4),(5,4),(6,4) → covers west wall x4, south wall partially\n\nNOT covered in starting room:\n- (6,4) and (8,4) - tiles adjacent to south wall (y5) at x4-8\n- But I also need to check: the south wall is at y5, x4-9. I need to search from a tile at y4 adjacent to the south wall.\n\nMiddle room (x15-25, y10-14):\n- I searched at (20,10), (20,12), (24,11)\n- (20,10) covers (19,9)-(21,11) → covers north wall x19-21 at y9\n- (20,12) covers (19,11)-(21,13) → covers interior\n- (24,11) covers (23,10)-(25,12) → covers east wall x25 at y10-12\n\nNOT covered in middle room:\n- North wall x15-18, x22-25 at y9\n- South wall x15-25 at y14\n- East wall x25 at y13\n- West wall x15 at y10, y12, y13\n\nRight room (x34-41, y3-9):\n- I searched at (35,4), (36,4), (37,6), (33,6), (35,8)\n- (35,4) covers (34,3)-(36,5) → covers north wall x34-36, west wall x34 at y3-5\n- (36,4) covers (35,3)-(37,5) → covers north wall x35-37\n- (37,6) covers (36,5)-(38,7) → covers east wall x41? No, x38 is adjacent. x41 is 3 tiles away.\n- (33,6) is outside the room in the corridor\n- (35,8) covers (34,7)-(36,9) → covers south wall x34-36, west wall x34 at y7-9\n\nNOT covered in right room:\n- North wall x38-41 at y3\n- South wall x37-41 at y9\n- East wall x41 at y4-8\n- West wall x34 at y6 (but that's a gap/door)\n\nLower-left room (x1-5, y13-17):\n- I searched at (3,13), (3,15)\n- (3,13) covers (2,12)-(4,14) → covers north wall x2-4 at y12, west wall x1? No, x1 is 2 tiles away from x3. Actually (2,12)-(4,14) means x2-4, y12-14. West wall x1 is not covered.\n- (3,15) covers (2,14)-(4,16) → covers south wall x2-4 at y16-17? Actually y16 is adjacent to y17 (south wall). (2,16),(3,16),(4,16) are adjacent to south wall (y17).\n\nNOT covered in lower-left room:\n- West wall x1 at y13-16 (need to search from x2)\n- South wall x1 at y17 (need to search from x2 at y16)\n- North wall x1, x5 at y12 (need to search from x2 or x4 at y13)\n- East wall x5 at y14, y16 (but these are gaps/doors)\n\nHmm, there are still some areas I haven't searched. Let me search at:\n1. (2,15) near the west wall of the lower-left room\n2. (2,13) near the north and west walls of the lower-left room\n3. (6,4) and (8,4) near the south wall of the starting room\n4. (38,4) near the east wall of the right room\n5. (38,8) near the east wall of the right room\n6. (17,13) and (23,13) near the south wall of the middle room\n\nLet me start with the ones I think are most likely: the south wall of the starting room, the east wall of the right room, and the south wall of the middle room.\n\nActually, let me also think about which walls could have a secret door that leads to a new area. Secret doors usually connect rooms to corridors or other rooms. \n\nLooking at the map:\n- The south wall of the starting room (y5, x4-9) is adjacent to the corridor at (3,5) and (10,5). But the wall itself is solid. A secret door here could lead to a corridor going down.\n- The east wall of the right room (x41, y4-8) is at the edge of the explored area. A secret door here could lead to a new room to the east.\n- The south wall of the middle room (y14, x15-25) is solid. A secret door here could lead to a new room below.\n- The north wall of the middle room (y9, x15-25) is solid. A secret door here could lead to a new room above.\n\nLet me search at these locations. Let me start with the south wall of the middle room, since there's a large unexplored area below and to the right of it.\n\nActually, wait - I just noticed something. Looking at the corridors more carefully, there's a corridor at (27,11) and (28,11) that seems to go to the east from the middle room. Let me check:\ny11: (27, '#'), (28, '#')\ny12: (26, '#'), (27, '#')\n\nSo (27,11) and (28,11) are corridors. (26,12) and (27,12) are corridors. These connect the east door of the middle room at (25,12) to the main east corridor at (27,10).\n\nBut (28,11) is a dead end! It doesn't connect to anything else. Let me check what's adjacent to (28,11):\n- (27,10) is `#` (corridor)\n- (28,10) is `#` (corridor)  \n- (29,10) is `#` (corridor)\n- (27,11) is `#` (corridor)\n- (28,11) is `#` (corridor)\n- (29,11) - is this a tile? Let me check... y11 doesn't have (29, anything).\n- (27,12) is `#` (corridor)\n- (28,12) - is this a tile? y12 doesn't have (28, anything).\n- (29,12) - y12 doesn't have (29, anything).\n\nSo (28,11) is adjacent to (27,10), (28,10), (29,10), (27,11), (27,12). The corridor continues to the right at y10 through (29,10), (30,10), (31,10), (32,10). So (28,11) is not a dead end - it connects to the main corridor at y10.\n\nOK, so all corridors are connected and explored. No dead ends except (8,0) at the top.\n\nLet me just search at the remaining unsearched wall positions. Let me start with the south wall of the starting room, the east wall of the right room, and the south wall of the middle room.\n\nActually, let me first try the east wall of the right room, since there's a large unexplored area to the east.",
